<section class="practical" id="{{ practical.anchor }}">
<p class="eyebrow">HANDS-ON PRACTICAL {{ practical.number }} OF {{ course.practicals.length }}</p>
<h4>Practical {{ practical.number }}: {{ practical.title }}</h4>
<p class="lead">Work with the real files for <code>{{ practical.target }}</code>.</p>
<aside class="callout"><strong>Before you start</strong>
<p>Open the script from the <code>scripts</code> folder in RStudio, or paste it into a new R Script tab. Keep this page on one side of the screen and RStudio on the other. Select one numbered block at a time and press <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Enter</kbd>.</p>
</aside>
<h5>What are we doing?</h5>
<p>{{ practical.method }}</p>
<h5>Why does it matter?</h5>
<p>{{ practical.why }}</p>
<h5>What data will we use?</h5>
<dl class="file-list">
{% for file in practical.files %}
<dt><code>{{ file[1] }}</code></dt><dd>{{ file[2] }}</dd>
{% endfor %}
{% if practical.extraPaths %}<dt>Training event raster</dt><dd>The change-class map identified by the project’s example settings. It is read directly from the participant ZIP.</dd>{% endif %}
</dl>
<p><strong>For a full replay</strong> {{ practical.rebuildInputs }}</p>
<h5>How does it work?</h5>
<ol>{% for step in practical.steps %}<li>{{ step }}</li>{% endfor %}</ol>
<p class="formula">{{ practical.formula }}</p>
<h5>What do the results mean?</h5>
<p>{{ practical.result }}</p>
{% for figure in practical.figures %}
<figure class="example">
<img src="assets/{{ practical.course }}/{{ figure[0] }}" alt="{{ figure[1] }}" loading="lazy">
<figcaption>{{ figure[1] }}</figcaption>
</figure>
{% endfor %}
{% if practical.folder == "03-cbi-plan" %}
<figure class="example"><div class="sample-chart" role="img" aria-label="The reviewed plan includes 100 calibration plots and 200 independent accuracy points.">
<p>Calibration · <strong>100 plots</strong></p><div class="sample-bar half"></div>
<p>Independent accuracy · <strong>200 points</strong></p><div class="sample-bar"></div>
</div><figcaption>Planned sample sizes from the reviewed CBI design.</figcaption></figure>
{% endif %}
<h5>How can Bhutan use this evidence?</h5>
<p>{{ practical.use }}</p>
<h5>Run one block at a time</h5>
<ol class="block-guide">
{% for block in practical.blocks %}
<li><strong>Block {{ block.number }} · {{ block.title }}</strong>
<p>{{ block.purpose }}</p><p><b>What to look for</b> {{ block.expected }}</p></li>
{% endfor %}
</ol>
<h5>Complete R script</h5>
<p>Paste once into <strong>File → New File → R Script</strong>. Save your copy anywhere inside the open project. The relative file paths start from the project folder.</p>
<div class="code-tools"><button class="button" type="button" data-copy="code-{{ practical.anchor }}">Copy All Code</button>
<a href="{{ practical.path }}" download>Download the .R file</a>
<span class="copy-status" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
<pre><code id="code-{{ practical.anchor }}">{{ practical.code | escape }}</code></pre>
<h5>Explain what you found</h5>
<p>{{ practical.question }}</p>
</section>
